 "summary": "Withdrawn: making `bigCellMul_apply` a simp lemma would make simp always unfold `bigCellMul`, which breaks the simp normal form of `bigCellMul_inj`, `bigCellMul_eq_one`, `bigCellMul_one` and `map_bigCellMul`, so keeping the term folded and expanding it only on request is the correct design. The rest of the subsystem, positive, negative and big-cell API is complete, keeps definition bodies hidden and carries consistent annotations.",
